  "result": "Perfect! All 219 tests pass. The credit note system is complete:\n\n\u2705 **Created src/credits.js:**\n- `nextCreditNoteNumber(existingNumbers, date)` \u2014 generates CN-<year>-<counter> format\n  - Independent counter from invoices (CN prefix)\n  - Resets counter each year\n  - Ignores invoice numbers in the existing numbers array\n\n- `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` \u2014 creates a credit note for refunds\n  - Only for invoices with status 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid'\n  - Validates amount is positive integer (error: AMOUNT_INVALID)\n  - Validates date in YYYY-MM-DD format (error: DATE_INVALID)\n  - Validates amount \u2264 invoice total (error: CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n  - Returns ok(creditNote) with { number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date }\n\n\u2705 **Added error codes:**\n- NOT_ISSUED \u2014 for draft invoices\n- AMOUNT_INVALID \u2014 for invalid amounts\n- CREDIT_TOO_HIGH \u2014 for amounts exceeding invoice total\n\n\u2705 **Tests (16 new):**\n- nextCreditNoteNumber: generation, incrementing, year rollover, unordered input\n- createCreditNote: issued/partially_paid/paid invoices, draft rejection\n- Amount validation: zero, negative, fractional amounts\n- Date validation: invalid formats\n- Credit limit enforcement: exact amount, exceeding amount\n- Independent numbering from invoices\n- Multiple invoices with sequential credit notes\n- Complex scenario with discounts and VAT\n\n**All 219 tests passing** across invoices, payments, dates, statements, and credit notes.",
